<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<StringTableFile xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <Name>conversations\x_labyrinth\x1131_memoryobject3</Name>
  <NextEntryID>1</NextEntryID>
  <EntryCount>36</EntryCount>
  <Entries>
    <Entry>
      <ID>1</ID>
      <DefaultText>Your fingers are twitching. Your mind races. Each blink sends branching streams of white fire across the inside of your eyelids. 

You can't deny it: you feel stronger and sharper - more *whole* - than when you landed here. 

Captive light swirls mockingly beneath the thick surface of the orb before you, obscuring shadows - memories - behind it. You will need to claim them somehow if you are to be free of this place, and find your companion. 
</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>2</ID>
      <DefaultText>Your city rises around you in a vision, burning under attack.

The defenders have fought and died all day. Still the attackers come, as if commanded to destroy you. They care nothing for mercy, surrender, or plunder - only *blood*.

Your keen-eyed companion has seen how to stop them from atop the tower. You must get her to safety and rally the defenders.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>3</ID>
      <DefaultText>You have already breached the orb, and discovered the memory within. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>4</ID>
      <DefaultText>As you turn toward the tower door, two attackers descend from a hovering machine before you can strike.

A giant carries a vibrating axe. His slim companion wears glassy armor and holds an invisible, sizzling blade.

Your companion backs away - she's too young to help. The attackers advance single file along the narrow parapet.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>5</ID>
      <DefaultText>Trade blows with the giant. You can handle it... for at least a strike or two.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>6</ID>
      <DefaultText>Duck under the giant's swing and attack before he can strike.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>7</ID>
      <DefaultText>Fight defensively, and figure out who presents the greater threat.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>8</ID>
      <DefaultText>The giant strikes twice in a blur. You block once, then fall to your knees, dazed. Your armor holds. As he raises the axe to finish you, you drive your blade beneath his breastplate and out through the back of his neck. Blood washes your hands. He falls, taking your weapon with him - and his companion attacks!</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>9</ID>
      <DefaultText>You duck her thrust; the wall behind you hisses, destroyed. Her next swing ruins your breastplate. She only needs to touch you with that blade.

As she draws back, you charge, driving her over the wall. She falls screaming, fifty meters to the ground.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>10</ID>
      <DefaultText>You hurry down the tower stairs to rejoin your allies. The door below stands slightly ajar; you hear more enemy soldiers beyond.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>11</ID>
      <DefaultText>You roll beneath the axe. He's fast, but you're faster. Overconfident, he hasn't committed to the attack.

As he raises the axe to finish you, you drive your blade beneath his breastplate and out through the back of his neck. Blood washes your hands. He falls, taking your weapon with him - and his companion attacks!</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>12</ID>
      <DefaultText>The memory seems clear: the woman's invisible blade is the greater threat. Its wavering field suggests it cuts at the molecular level, unmaking matter. She waits behind the giant, unable to strike past him. Your best chance is to tackle her first.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>13</ID>
      <DefaultText>She expects the giant to handle you; her attention is on your ward. You dive between his legs and rise inside her guard, driving your dagger beneath her chin before she can strike.

You catch her before the blade falls on you, then swing her around. It cuts the giant in two.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>14</ID>
      <DefaultText>Hurl yourself against the door and knock them to the ground. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>15</ID>
      <DefaultText>Crack the door open to sneak past them.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>16</ID>
      <DefaultText>Charge through them, counting on your defenses to protect you. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>17</ID>
      <DefaultText>You charge through the shadows and slam your shoulder into the door.

It bursts open, scattering two soldiers. You rush through and cut them down before they recover.

Blood pools in the hall.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>18</ID>
      <DefaultText>You ease the gleaming door open. It squeaks like a bell in your memory, and you freeze. The soldiers keep talking. You squeeze through and creep down the bloodstained hall.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>19</ID>
      <DefaultText>You burst through the door and ram the first soldier. He falls. His companion's blow hurls you down the hall - just as you hoped.

Your ears ring, but your chest barely aches. You rise and run as projectiles spark around you. A bolt glances off your reinforced backplate.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>20</ID>
      <DefaultText>The memory fades, returning you to your body.

Your temples throb. The memories blaze within you like a mountaintop bonfire, visible to every predator for kilometers around.

A tremor rocks the floor. Swaying, you glimpse frantic movement inside the mirror at the room's edge.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>21</ID>
      <DefaultText>Coax the shadows to the front of the glass so you can see them.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>22</ID>
      <DefaultText />
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>23</ID>
      <DefaultText>Walk away from the orb.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>24</ID>
      <DefaultText>Speaking quietly, you call a slender shadow to the surface of the glass, into the light. It is a young woman, bound in chains of sorrow.

She speaks quietly of a memory. You lean in, closer and closer, until her whispered words fill your mind...

{SOUND: Wordless whisper.}</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>25</ID>
      <DefaultText>You batter the orb with your fists until cracks spread across the glass, growing and joining.

Light leaks through the cracks like blood, filling your eyes with the orb's radiance, and your mind with another memory...

{SOUND: Fists hitting glass, followed by cracking.}</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>26</ID>
      <DefaultText />
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>27</ID>
      <DefaultText>Crack the orb with your fists.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>28</ID>
      <DefaultText>Jerk away again.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>29</ID>
      <DefaultText>You shout at the orb until a hulking shadow strides to the surface of the glass, into the light. It is a hideous creature, a giant, and it is grinning. Its bloodstained claws leap through the surface of the glass and close over your head.

Even in the attempt, you feel your confidence growing, and a memory rises in the crushing darkness...</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>30</ID>
      <DefaultText>Your confidence grows. Speaking quietly, you call a slender shadow to the surface of the glass, into the light. It is a young woman, bound in chains of sorrow, and you almost remember her name before she meets your eyes. 

She speaks quietly of a memory. You lean in, closer and closer, until her whispered words fill your mind...

{SOUND: Wordless whisper.}</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>31</ID>
      <DefaultText>You shout at the orb, calling to the shadows within. Soon, they are *all* flowing towards the surface of the orb. You reel back, but is too late. They smash through the glass, and envelop you. 

Eyes - the eyes of those you lost - hold you, frozen and helpless. Hulking shadows claw at your throat. Slender blades cut at your heels, and you sink, deeper and deeper, into darkness.

Even as you sink, you feel your confidence grow, and a memory rises that was, perhaps, best forgotten...</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>32</ID>
      <DefaultText>You dash your knuckles against the orb, bruising the glowing surface but not breaking it. Even so, you feel yourself becoming stronger.

Shadows flow from the center of the orb, making the contusions shift and flow, forming images that fill your mind with another memory...

{SOUND: Fists dully hitting glass, no crack.}</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>33</ID>
      <DefaultText>With increased power, you smash the glass with a single blow, and the light coils up around your arm and plunges into your heart, filling it with another memory...

{SOUND: Shatter.}</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>34</ID>
      <DefaultText>Your frenzied punches draw your own blood but leave no mark on the shining glass. Even so, you feel yourself becoming stronger.

Panting, you pause for breath, and watch as curious shadows, perhaps drawn by the ruckus you've made, drift up from the center of the orb.

Twisting and snarling, they paint themselves across the surface in patterns that suffuse your mind with another memory...

{SOUND: Fists dully hitting glass, no crack.}</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>35</ID>
      <DefaultText />
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>36</ID>
      <DefaultText />
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
  </Entries>
</StringTableFile>